            "body": "@kkHuang-amd @1am9trash quick update on this one. #38293 removed prefill CP on HIP, --enable-prefill-cp now errors out on ROCm at arg validation, so the path this fixes isnt reachable on main anymore and the branch conflicts. Nothing to merge here right now, and a rebase wouldn't change that.\n\nThe bug itself still matters for the CP refactor though: on gfx950 the fused DSA rope+cache kernel ropes the local q shard and the gathered full K with the same local positions, which corrupted KV and garbled output. If HIP prefill CP comes back on that fused path, rope has to happen before the gather. Is someone on the AMD side tracking the HIP CP refactor? If so I'll close this and point them here.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-02T16:18:05Z",
            "databaseId": 5956496297,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-02T16:18:05Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/32098#issuecomment-5956496297"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "reger-men"
            },
            "body": "Closing this one. #38293 removed the legacy prefill CP on HIP, and since #34200 `--enable-prefill-cp` on ROCm is only accepted for DeepSeek-V4 on its own dsv4 backend. So the gfx950 DSA MLA path this fixes isnt reachable on main anymore, and the branch conflicts with main by now. The bug itself (on gfx950 the fused DSA rope + cache kernel ropes the gathered full K with the local shard's positions) will come back if prefill CP returns for the DSA models on ROCm through the new CP stack, and I'll redo the fix on top of that when it does.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-27T13:00:16Z",
